WEBVTT

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.470
Well, I'm Hatonami Renjiro.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:14.700
I'm the head of the Hatonami Union, 
 a small group of yakuza.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.380
I was locked up for about 
five years, I think.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:24.410
My time in the slammer was supposed 
to last a little longer, though.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.810
As for how I got caught?

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.150
Well, don't ask such rude questions.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.750
The details aren't important anyway.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:43.540
I was stuck eating shitty food  
when that Gibia crisis happened.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.880
The officers who were supposed 
to be running the place

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.020
were no match for monsters.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:56.610
It was actually safer in the cells.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:03.450
The officers went down first, 
 leaving nothing but crooks.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:09.930
At that point, escape wasn't so hard, you know.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:15.240
Gibia are dead men. We're the living.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:19.810
I've heard Gibia run on instincts 
they had when they were human.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:23.090
The urge to breed, was it?

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:31.480
Seeing dead men running on instinct, 
fighting even harder to survive than the living...

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:36.040
Talk about karma in this world.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:42.800
Though, maybe struggling like that
 is the real nature of humans.

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:45.760
That good enough?

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:51.620
Ow.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:02.270
<i>I'm so sorry, everyone!</i>

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.190
<i>I'm finished!</i>

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.700
<b>"Desperate Situation"</b>

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:00.800
Kathleen!

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.740
Are you all right, Kathleen?

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:07.220
Oh, my.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:11.590
All right. How about this, then?

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.000
Hup!

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.740
So high!

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:22.140
I see our princess is in a good mood now.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.010
Out of my way! Move!

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:48.390
Kathleen!

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:01.550
Kathleen?

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:51.180
Okay. Time to clean house.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.570
Papa! Papa!

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:37.860
I'm heading out.

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:41.610
Take care, Robert.

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:49.680
When I get back, let's go see 
your father and mother back in Japan.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.760
It's been a while since we last saw them.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.060
Papa, off to work?

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:58.950
That's right.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:00.890
I'll be back in a while.

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:04.630
Do your best to help your mama.

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:06.090
Yes!

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:10.350
Good girl. I love you.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:18.320
Papa! Have a safe trip!

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.900
I'll be back!

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.880
Mama, don't cry.

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:36.600
Kathleen.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.360
Did you hear?

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:44.450
Apparently he got shot by a stray bullet 
while photographing a battlefield.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.440
How unfortunate.

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:55.130
His daughter is still so young, too.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.860
Apparently they're going back 
to Japan after the funeral.

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:10.550
Kathleen, always keep your chin up in life.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:13.640
Yeah.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:17.510
When you look at the history of Earth,

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:21.730
there's never any disaster 
or war that doesn't end.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.410
Every night comes to an end.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:27.800
What if something bad happens?

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:31.350
It won't last forever.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:36.080
The spot where you fell 
doesn't hurt anymore, does it?

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:38.880
You're right!

00:08:55.710 --> 00:09:00.010
I'm... alive?

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:15.420
U-Um, who are you?

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:19.950
I'm Ayame. Former cop.

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:22.520
A cop?

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:27.040
I'm Kathleen. Thank you for saving me.

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:30.610
Save it for after, 
when we're actually in the clear.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.870
Is there anyone else inside?

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:38.620
My mother and my friends are still in there.

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:46.890
Damn it, I can't make any progress!

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.190
<i>Kathleen's in trouble!</i>

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.390
Kathleen!

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:53.320
I pray you're still safe!

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:56.370
I'm coming to rescue you!

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.010
Sensui!

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:19.410
Eat this!

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.440
Are you all okay?!

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:58.590
What?!

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:18.350
Why, you...!

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:49.060
Take that!

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:14.960
Try this on for size!

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:25.890
I didn't think they were so...

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:28.300
Hmm.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:39.600
It's finally over.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:43.040
That reminded me of fighting Oda's army.

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:45.770
That was a crazy amount of them.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:52.410
Hey, Sensui, you still think monsters 
are easier than cutting down people?

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:55.850
Everyone!

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:00.880
I'm so glad you're safe!

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:04.740
Oh, Kathleen!

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:08.890
Who might you be?

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:10.130
Huh?

00:13:10.130 --> 00:13:12.030
Oh, uh...

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:16.650
She's Ayame-san. A former cop.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:20.350
She saved me when 
I was in trouble a moment ago.

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:21.890
Really?

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:28.160
Ayame-san, thank you so much 
for saving my daughter.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:32.430
No, I just did the right thing.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:37.090
Ayame-san, are you all alone?

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:41.320
We're heading towards Niigata,

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:43.290
but would you like to come with us?

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:44.310
Huh?

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:46.930
That's a great idea! You should!

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:53.430
Having a strong person like you 
accompany us would be reassuring.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:57.810
Gotta have companions when you travel, 
and compassion in life.

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:02.690
Ahh, I'm so glad you were rescued, Kathleen.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:05.870
Guess that works, too.

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:12.700
Nice to have you with us, Ayame-san!

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:14.740
Same.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.790
It's good to have you, Ayame-san.

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:22.780
We'll be at a disadvantage 
if we're surrounded in this tunnel,

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:24.960
so let's get out of here at once.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:28.590
Finding a place we can rest 
would be preferable.

00:14:31.490 --> 00:14:33.940
You guys see that?

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:39.390
Those guys... I knew they 
weren't just ordinary people.

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:43.980
Yes. That was some
terrifying combat potential.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.400
The facilities are old,

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:07.400
but it's a pretty good hot spring.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:10.000
I've been here once before.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:11.820
Wow.

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:16.660
I'm just grateful we can take a bath.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:17.760
Right?!

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:20.380
Let's get going!

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:22.430
Uh, pardon me.

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:24.640
The men's bath is over there.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:27.110
Well, I guess you're right.

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:33.080
Phew, this is refreshing.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:37.510
How many years has it been
since we visited a hot spring?

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:38.560
I know.

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:42.010
<i>Those are incredible scars...</i>

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:45.130
<i>I know she said she used to be a cop,</i>

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:49.720
<i>but I'm sure Ayame-san's been 
fighting against the Gibia, too.</i>

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:51.320
What?

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:54.270
Just thinking you're really muscular.

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:58.400
You must have been through a lot, Ayame-san.

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:01.390
Oh, well, uh...

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:04.270
It's good to see you two get along so well.

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:06.230
You think?

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:10.310
Maybe it's because it's always 
been just the two of us.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.700
What about your parents?

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:18.480
My mother was killed by Gibia.

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:25.600
Ayame, make sure you 
stick to an honest life.

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:30.560
Yeah. I won't turn out like Dad.

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:34.050
I see. I'm sorry.

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:37.970
My father was a hopeless man.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:42.840
He was yakuza, and I have 
no idea what he's doing now.

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:44.140
Huh?!

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:49.850
He caused some kind of incident, 
and I know he got thrown in jail for it.

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:53.160
I was planning to arrest him myself...

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:56.380
That's why you became 
a police officer, isn't it.

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:03.470
He doesn't matter now.

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:10.670
I can feel the fatigue blowing away.

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:13.730
Paradise, paradise.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:17.170
Hot springs help wounds heal faster, too,

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:21.760
so you really should take 
a long soak, Sensui-kun.

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:25.850
That's the same thing my Master once said.

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.520
Oh?

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:30.050
Sensui's master, huh?

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:36.690
I must say, I'm very interested in 
the master of the Slayer of Thousands.

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:41.330
I bet he was a really skilled man.

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:43.970
I'll be heading back first.

00:17:52.470 --> 00:17:54.510
Those are incredible scars.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:57.790
They're old scars. Don't worry about them.

00:18:02.270 --> 00:18:05.450
Never heard of any old 
scars looking that fresh.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.850
He's being a man.

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:54.270
Boy, I'm on your side.

00:18:56.000 --> 00:19:00.610
I'm sorry I couldn't save 
your mother and your father.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.570
What's your name?

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:05.870
Sensui.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:20.580
<i>In the warring states era,</i>

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:24.910
<i>fierce battles for dominance of 
the land took place in every region.</i>

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:30.060
<i>The greatest force in the Kyuushuu 
region was the Ootomo Clan</i>

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:33.940
<i>and, as their vassals, the Kanzaki Clan 
was raided and destroyed</i>

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.420
<i>in a night raid on Shimazu.</i>

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:43.960
<i>The sole survivor, Sensui, was adopted 
by Halbert and raised as a swordsman.</i>

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:50.620
Sensui, hot springs help 
wounds heal faster, too.

00:19:51.060 --> 00:19:52.850
Why is that?

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:57.460
Because it warms your body and 
enhances its regenerative functions.

00:19:57.740 --> 00:19:58.640
Yes!

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:02.750
You should gather 
as much knowledge as you can.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:05.680
That's part of growing up.

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:08.210
Yes, master.

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:09.430
Sensui.

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:14.670
No matter what happens in life, 
 there's always a reason.

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:18.440
Even if we don't understand it right now,
 we'll understand in time.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:20.810
I understand.

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:28.410
However, even hot springs 
won't help my disease.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:34.700
Please hang in there! Master!

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:39.280
Sensui.

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:46.690
Live, Sensui.

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:50.050
Master? Master?

00:20:56.090 --> 00:21:01.850
<i>In 1587, the Shimazu Clan 
plotted their conquest of Kyuushuu</i>

00:21:01.850 --> 00:21:06.110
<i>and invaded Bungo no Kuni 
to attack the Ootomo Clan.</i>

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:09.620
<i>The head of the Ootomo, Ootomo Sourin,</i>

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:12.400
<i>called for reinforcements from Hideyoshi.</i>

00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:19.340
<i>One of the Daimyo from the Toyotomi 
alliance sent to their aid in Kyuushuu</i>

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:25.300
<i>was Matsumoto Jouzen, 
the man Sensui later came to serve.</i>

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:34.490
<i>However, the Shimazu army was fierce,</i>

00:21:34.490 --> 00:21:38.610
<i>and Ootomo suffered a great loss 
alongside their reinforcements.</i>

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:41.960
<i>Sensui himself served as the rear guard</i>

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:47.020
<i>to allow Matsumoto Jouzen's army 
to escape from Kyuushuu.</i>

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:52.890
So you're known as Sensui.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:55.660
Your feats during this battle were splendid.

00:21:56.060 --> 00:21:59.950
I had something interesting presented to me.

00:21:59.950 --> 00:22:02.130
I hear it's called Suigetsumaru.

00:22:03.410 --> 00:22:05.480
I'm giving it to you.

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:15.110
I hear this sword can cut even 
the moon reflected on water.

00:22:15.760 --> 00:22:19.590
With this and the sword 
I received from my master,

00:22:19.590 --> 00:22:21.860
I would like to perfect my dual wielding.

00:22:25.310 --> 00:22:26.520
<i>Master...</i>

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:32.050
<i>I'm sure there must have been a reason for me 
to come to this era, too, wasn't there?</i>

00:22:33.460 --> 00:22:34.690
Sensui.

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:37.870
We'll be heading out soon.

00:22:53.090 --> 00:22:54.620
Is that...?

00:22:54.620 --> 00:22:56.000
What's the matter?

00:22:57.830 --> 00:23:00.100
It would seem we're being followed.

00:23:00.100 --> 00:23:01.300
Huh?!

00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:06.670
Dad?!

00:23:11.530 --> 00:23:13.870
<b>"Dream Road to Death"</b>
